    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A detached three-bedroom property situated in the peaceful rural setting of Kilballyowen, Aughrim, Co. Wicklow.\r\n\r\nThe property offers an excellent opportunity for buyers seeking a home in a tranquil countryside location, with the potential to modernise and refurbish to suit individual requirements. The accommodation comprises three bedrooms and one bathroom, together with living and kitchen areas.\r\nThe property is currently vacant and may appeal to owner-occupiers, investors, or those looking for a renovation project in a scenic part of County Wicklow.\r\n\r\nThe property may be eligible for the Vacant Home Scheme which is a government scheme that provides financial support to help people bring long-term vacant or derelict properties back into use as homes.\r\n\r\nSet within the Aughrim area, the property benefits from a quiet rural environment while remaining within reach of local amenities and services. The surrounding countryside provides an attractive setting for those looking to enjoy the lifestyle and natural beauty for which County Wicklow is renowned.\r\n\r\n\r\nThe information contained in this brochure is provided in good faith and is believed to be accurate at the time of publication. While every reasonable effort has been made to ensure its accuracy, some details may have been supplied by the vendor and have not been independently verified.\r\nProspective purchasers are advised that no structural, boundary, measured or topographical survey has been carried out by the Auctioneers or on behalf of the Vendor in connection with this property.\r\nThe measurements, dimensions, areas and boundaries contained in these particulars are provided for guidance purposes only and should not be relied upon as being accurate. Prospective purchasers are strongly advised to satisfy themselves independently as to the condition, dimensions, boundaries, extent and suitability of the property prior to entering into any contract.\r\nThe Auctioneers and Vendor accept no responsibility for any inaccuracies, omissions or discrepancies arising from the information provided. All prospective purchasers should make their own enquiries and, where appropriate, obtain independent professional advice and carry out any surveys or inspections they consider necessary."
      },
